# Map data — CC BY-SA 3.0

`territories.json` and `sea-routes.json` in this directory are derived from
[`Risk_board.svg`](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Risk_board.svg) by
**Gr0gmint**, published on Wikimedia Commons under
[CC BY-SA 3.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/) (dual-licensed
GFDL at the author's option).

The territory outlines were extracted from that SVG and re-baked into JSON, which
makes them an adaptation. Under share-alike they remain CC BY-SA 3.0: you may copy,
distribute and modify them provided you keep this attribution and license any
derivative of them on the same terms.

This is deliberately **not** the MIT license that covers the rest of the repository.

`board.json` (adjacency, continent bonuses, display names) is not derived from the
SVG — it encodes the standard Risk board topology, which is a fact rather than a
creative work.
